para.p:
We consider an agent interacting with an environment over a sequence of steps;
at each time t𝑡t the agent receives an observation ot∈𝒪subscript𝑜𝑡𝒪o_{t}\in\mathcal{O} from the environment
and then sends an action at∈𝒜subscript𝑎𝑡𝒜a_{t}\in\mathcal{A} to the environment.

At each point in time our method maintains a policy π:𝒪→𝒜:𝜋→𝒪𝒜\pi:\mathcal{O}\rightarrow\mathcal{A}
and a reward function estimate r^:𝒪×𝒜→ℝ:^𝑟→𝒪𝒜ℝ\hat{r}:\mathcal{O}\times\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\mathbb{R},
each parametrized by deep neural networks.

We select pairs of segments (σ1,σ2)superscript𝜎1superscript𝜎2\left(\sigma^{1},\sigma^{2}\right)
from the trajectories {τ1,…,τi}superscript𝜏1…superscript𝜏𝑖\{\tau^{1},\ldots,\tau^{i}\} produced in step 1,
and send them to a human for comparison.
